diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <title>Modern CSS Font Metric Normalization</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <main>
+    <header>
+      <h1>Typography &amp; Visual Height Normalization</h1>
+      <p>Demonstrating automatic font metric normalization and locked numeric metric overrides with modern CSS <code>font-size-adjust</code>.</p>
+    </header>
+
+    <section id="mixed-fonts-container">
+      <span class="badge">font-size-adjust: from-font</span>
+      <h2>Mixed Fonts Container</h2>
+      <p>
+        When mixing proportional prose fonts with inline technical elements like <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code>, <code>const scale = 1.0;</code>, or <code>Array.prototype.map()</code>, different typefaces naturally exhibit different aspect ratios (the ratio of lowercase <em>x-height</em> to total font size).
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        By applying <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code> on <code>#mixed-fonts-container</code>, the browser automatically computes the primary font's metric ratio and scales inline <code>&lt;code&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;kbd&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;samp&gt;</code> elements so their lowercase glyphs share a seamless visual height with surrounding prose.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section id="independent-theme-container">
+      <span class="badge">font-size-adjust: ex-height 0.52</span>
+      <h2>Independent Theme Container</h2>
+      <p>
+        This standalone theme container (<code>#independent-theme-container</code>) enforces a strict, predictable visual proportion regardless of which system or web font is active by specifying an explicit metric and numeric override: <code>font-size-adjust: ex-height 0.52</code>.
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        Both body copy and embedded code tokens such as <code>theme.lockMetrics(0.52)</code> and <code>--metric-ratio: 0.52</code> are normalized to a locked x-height aspect value of <code>0.52</code>, preventing layout shifts and preserving visual harmony across themes.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+</body>
+</html>
